{comment}
  The FIRST-RUN panel (decided 2026-10-20): the platform draws it in the section's frame while the section has
  no index page; creating one replaces it. This theme's look for it; the platform ships a plain one.
{endcomment}
{comment}
  THE FIRST-RUN BLOCK. It answers the only two questions a person has in
  the first two minutes -- did it work, and where do I go next -- and it is
  deliberately the page's CONTENT slot rather than a banner bolted on top:
  the moment anyone writes a front page, this disappears on its own.
  Nothing to find, nothing to switch off, no setting to discover.

  That is also why it is not styled like a designed page. A default that
  looks like a design decision is one a new user starts trying to remove
  instead of replace.
{endcomment}
<div class="py-5">
  <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm">
    <div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">
      <p class="text-uppercase text-secondary small fw-semibold mb-2">Default page</p>
      <h1 class="h4 mb-3">Your installation is working.</h1>
      <p class="mb-4">
        CoolMS shows this until the site has a front page. Create an index page
        for the site and it takes this panel's place.
      </p>
      {comment}The admin link only to a signed-in admin (decided 2026-10-20); a stranger sees the source link.{endcomment}
      <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
        {if:user.isAdmin}<a href="/admin" class="btn btn-primary">Open the admin</a>{endif}
        <a href="https://github.com/coolms" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Source and packages</a>
      </div>
      {if:user.isAdmin}
      <p class="text-secondary small mb-0">
        The front page is an index page under <strong>Content</strong>.
        Everything else on this page — the header, the footer — comes from the
        active theme.
      </p>
      {endif}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
